 of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $607M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.37\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield of 4.9% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 70% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6967277877641688},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.1M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2078547.58},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Industrials peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (42% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Jacobs Solutions Inc. $J Stock: Lido Advisors LLC Trims Stake","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/17/jacobs-solutions-inc-j-stock-lido-advisors-llc-trims-stake.html","date":"2026-11-17","timestamp":1794934081.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.917,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"How to Earn $500 a Month From Jacobs Solutions Stock Ahead of Q4 Earnings","source":"benzinga.com","link":"https://www.benzinga.com/trading-ideas/dividends/26/11/63467629/how-to-earn-500-a-month-from-jacobs-solutions-stock-ahead-of-q4-earnings","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795178552.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.178,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Jacobs Solutions EVP William B. Allen Jr. Sells 81 Shares for Tax Purposes","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/jacobs-solutions-evp-william-b-allen-jr-sells-81-shares-for-tax-purposes","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795128836.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Jacobs Solutions CFO Venkatesh Nathamuni Surrenders 741 Shares at $158.23 for RSU Tax Withholding","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/jacobs-solutions-cfo-venkatesh-nathamuni-surrenders-741-shares-at-15823-for-rsu-tax-withholding","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795128819.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Jacobs Solutions CEO Robert V. Pragada Withholds 2,706 Shares at $157.24 for RSU Tax on November 18, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https:/